.TH CLOCWORK 1 "2026-09-18" "clocwork 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clocwork \- lines per language, AI co\-authored commits and token cost over a repository's history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clocwork
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIREPO\fR]
.br
.B clocwork tokens
[\-q] [\-o DIR] [REPO]
.br
.B clocwork render
[\-q] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] \-o DIR
.br
.B clocwork \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lines per language, AI co\-authored commits and token cost over a repository's history.
.PP
Every non\-merge commit reachable from the analysed ref is measured with
.BR cloc (1)
in git diff mode and cached per file, so a first run over a long history is slow and every later run takes seconds; merge commits carry no code of their own and are listed but not measured. The result is one
.I index.html
(its charts load Chart.js and its plugins from a CDN) plus a
.I commit_bodies.js
sidecar, written to a workspace next to the repository, never inside it: lines per language and type at every commit, which commits an AI agent co\-authored and when each model first appeared, and, when a coding agent's logs for the repository are on the machine (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, OpenCode), what the work cost in tokens.
.PP
A first argument that is not a command is taken as
.IR REPO ,
so
.B clocwork ~/code/foo
works; the default is the current directory, and any directory inside the repository will do.
.SH OPTIONS
Options more than one command takes. Each command's own options follow it below.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
print nothing but errors
.TP
.B \-\-config PATH
explicit clocwork.toml. Taken by run and render.
.TP
.B \-\-locale TAG
region locale for the page (default: $CLOCWORK_LOCALE, else the machine's region). Taken by run and render.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-open
do not open the dashboard in a browser. Taken by run and render.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output DIR
workspace directory (default: <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats). Taken by run and tokens.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS run
.B clocwork run
[\-q] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] [\-o DIR] [\-\-branch REF] [\-\-max\-commits N] [\-j N] [\-\-no\-tokens] [\-\-cache\-dir DIR] [REPO]
.PP
analyse, archive tokens and render (the default)
.TP
.I REPO
repository or any directory inside it (default: cwd)
.TP
.B \-\-branch REF
ref to analyse (default: the checked\-out branch)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-commits N
measure at most N uncached commits this run
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs N
cloc processes to run at once (default: one per CPU core)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tokens
skip the agent log scan
.TP
.B \-\-cache\-dir DIR
cache location (default: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/clocwork, else ~/.cache/clocwork; wins over both)
.SS tokens
.B clocwork tokens
[\-q] [\-o DIR] [REPO]
.PP
archive agent token logs only
.TP
.I REPO
repository or any directory inside it (default: cwd)
.SS render
.B clocwork render
[\-q] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-locale TAG] [\-\-no\-open] \-o DIR
.PP
re\-render the dashboard from existing workspace data
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output DIR
the workspace to render
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLOCWORK_LOCALE
A BCP 47 tag such as
.BR en\-SE .
The region locale the page formats numbers, dates and units with. Wins over the machine's setting;
.B \-\-locale
wins over both.
.TP
.B CODEX_HOME
Where Codex CLI keeps its sessions, read from its
.I sessions/
and
.I archived_sessions/
directories; the default is
.IR ~/.codex .
.TP
.B GEMINI_CLI_HOME
The directory Gemini CLI uses in place of the home directory; its sessions are read from
.I .gemini/tmp/
and
.I .cache/.gemini/tmp/
below it.
.TP
.B OPENCODE_DB
An OpenCode database to read besides every
.I opencode*.db
in its data directory; absolute, or relative to that directory.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
When set, the cloc cache lives under
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/clocwork/ ;
otherwise under
.IR ~/.cache/clocwork/ .
.B \-\-cache\-dir
wins over both. Only
.B run
uses the cache.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Where OpenCode keeps its sessions, read from
.I opencode/
below it; the default is
.I ~/.local/share
on every system, OpenCode having no variable of its own.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <repo\-parent>/<repo\-name>\-stats/
The workspace: a sibling of the repository, overridden with
.BR \-o .
.TP
.I clocwork.json
Which repository the workspace belongs to. A run against another repository is refused rather than overwriting the workspace.
.TP
.I clocwork.toml
Optional configuration: page title, test\-path rules, extra agents. The first found wins:
.BR \-\-config ,
then this file in the workspace, then
.I .clocwork.toml
in the repository.
.TP
.I token_usage.json
The per\-day token archive, kept per agent, read from coding agents' logs. It cannot be regenerated once the logs expire; no run shrinks it.
.TP
.I full_commit_data.json
The analysis the page is rendered from, with the clocwork version that made it, and its commit when run from a clone. The page's footer names the build that rendered it.
.TP
.IR index.html ", " commit_bodies.js
The dashboard and its sidecar of full commit messages.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/clocwork/<name>\-<hash>/cloc_cache.json
Per\-file cloc results keyed by commit, so a changed test rule or language table re\-reads the cache instead of re\-running cloc.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
An error the command reported: Python older than 3.11, cloc missing, older than 2.06 or failing, no git repository, a repository with no commits, a workspace belonging to another repository, invalid configuration, or an unreadable, unwritable or corrupt file. A usage error also exits 2, with the usage line on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cloc (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-log (1)
